      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining the Provider**\n\nI've decided to move forward with Google Cloud Vertex AI as the specific external provider. My focus is now on how to make this choice readily identifiable within the Python file and resolving that provider's resource. I'm considering the best way to structure the code for clarity and maintainability.\n\n\n**Implementing the Resolver**\n\nI'm now creating the `select_platform_resource.py` file and will define the `resolve_vertex_ai_model_resource` function. This function takes a model name or ID as input and constructs the appropriate resource name for a Vertex AI model, using the Google Cloud AI Platform imports. This process requires project, location, and model IDs as parameters.\n\n\n**Constructing the Resolver**\n\nNow, I'm generating the content for `select_platform_resource.py`. This will include an import from `google.cloud.aiplatform` to signal the provider. I'm also writing the `resolve_vertex_ai_model_resource` function, which will accept `project_id`, `location`, and `model_id` and return a formatted Vertex AI model resource string. I'm aiming for clarity and directness in its code.\n\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789866566799,
          "start": 1789866563647
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
